From: Ely Office
Subject: Writer compare counts both documents' changes as accepted

- Comparing two copies of a document with the same unaccepted
  changes still showed those changes, so a compare that found no new
  difference looked like one that did (#140).
- As Word does, .uno:CompareDocuments now accepts every tracked
  change in both documents before comparing: in the open one, and in
  the older one only when it was loaded for this compare (an older
  document already open elsewhere keeps its changes). Files on disk
  are not touched. The answer is still the count of differences, 0
  when none.

diff --git a/sw/source/uibase/uiview/view2.cxx b/sw/source/uibase/uiview/view2.cxx
--- a/sw/source/uibase/uiview/view2.cxx
+++ b/sw/source/uibase/uiview/view2.cxx
@@ -2967,7 +2967,17 @@
             m_pWrtShell->EnterStdMode(); // delete selections
 
             if( bCompare )
-                nFound = m_pWrtShell->CompareDoc( *static_cast<SwDocShell*>( xDocSh.get() )->GetDoc() );
+            {
+                // Ely: changes both already hold count as accepted, as in Word.
+                SwDoc& rOld = *static_cast<SwDocShell*>( xDocSh.get() )->GetDoc();
+                // Only a document loaded here for comparing; never an open one.
+                if( nRet == 2 )
+                    rOld.getIDocumentRedlineAccess().AcceptAllRedline( true );
+                else
+                    SAL_WARN("sw.ui", "compare: the older document is open, its changes stay");
+                m_pWrtShell->getIDocumentRedlineAccess().AcceptAllRedline( true );
+                nFound = m_pWrtShell->CompareDoc( rOld );
+            }
             else
                 nFound = m_pWrtShell->MergeDoc( *static_cast<SwDocShell*>( xDocSh.get() )->GetDoc() );
 
